course: dictionary
lesson: 13073
title: Festivity and festivities
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A festivity is a celebration, a time when people come together to have fun, often with music, food and parties. Festivities is the plural form, so you use it for the whole set of celebrations, or for more than one event. «The village held festivities for three days.» The clue is that it lasted three days, so festivities must mean the parties and fun events, not just one party.
explain: The word can also mean the feeling itself. «The hall was filled with an air of festivity.» Nobody says the hall is a party here. The clue is the air, which means the happy, joyful mood that a celebration brings. Festivity is uncountable, so we do not say a festivity or two festivities for the feeling.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping in party or celebration. «Join in the festivities» means join in the parties and fun. If the sentence still makes sense, you have got it. Festivities happen at Christmas, Diwali, Eid, Hanukkah, Chinese New Year, weddings and birthdays.
fact: Festivities are the parties, music, food and fun events held to celebrate something.
fact: Festivity, on its own, is the happy, joyful feeling of a celebration.
fact: Festivities is usually used in the plural, because a celebration often has many events.
fact: «The Christmas festivities» means the Christmas parties and fun.
fact: «An air of festivity» means a joyful, celebrating mood in a place.
exercise: «The village held festivities for three days to celebrate the harvest.» What are festivities here? | Tiring walks round the fields | Lost bags left on the bus | Lessons at the village school | *Parties, music and fun held to celebrate
exercise: «The shop was bright and full of festivity for the New Year.» What does festivity mean here? | Long queues at the bank | Sadness and worry | *A happy, joyful feeling of celebration | A broken window
exercise: Ravi says, «Diwali festivities are every autumn.» Which word could replace festivities without changing the meaning? | Homework | Mess | Holidays only | *Celebrations
test: Which sentence uses festivity to mean the joyful feeling? | «The bus was late again.» | «The festivities were held in the park.» | *«Everyone was smiling, and the hall buzzed with festivity.»
test: «Join in the festivities» means what? | To leave early without saying goodbye | To sit quietly alone | To write a letter to the council | *To take part in the parties and fun
exam: Which event is most likely to have festivities? | *A wedding with music, food and dancing | Sitting a maths test | Writing a shopping list | Cleaning out the car
